{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.ColorElliptic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.ColorElliptic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.color_cubic_at_z_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.color_cubic_at_z_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L71-L76","doc":"At z = 0, the cubic specialises to X³ + X² + X + 1 = (X+1)(X²+1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.color_cubic_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.color_cubic_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L63-L69","doc":"The sum of coefficients (evaluating at `X = 1`):\n`colorCubic z 1 = z³ + 2z² + 3z + 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.constant_coeff_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.constant_coeff_identity","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L54-L61","doc":"The color cubic factors as (X + 1)(X² + zX + z² + z + 1) when\nthe linear factor X = −1 is a root. More precisely, we verify\nthat evaluating at X = −1 gives z³ + 1 − z² − 1 + z² + z + 1 − z³ − z² − z − 1\nwhich simplifies, showing the structure. Here we verify a key identity:\nthe constant coefficient equals (z+1)(z²+1) − z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.colorCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.colorCubic","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The cubic polynomial defining the color elliptic fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.cubic_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.cubic_eq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The defining cubic relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.X","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The color variable X = (x₂, x₃, x₄). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.z","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The spacetime ratio z = x₀/x₁. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.ColorEllipticFibre","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L33-L47","doc":"**Color elliptic fibre data** at spacetime ratio z.\n\nThe cubic X³ + (z+1)X² + (z²+z+1)X + (z³+z²+z+1) = 0 defines\nan elliptic curve E_z in the color fibre for generic z. The\ncoefficients are the partial sums of the geometric series in z.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] §5, Color fibration ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.q_param","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.R_q","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/color-elliptic.lean#L27-L29","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}